;; The price book for dougaka. DATA, not code — ADR-2608110200 決定 3.
;;
;; ## Denominated on a TESTNET, on purpose
;;
;; Every plan here settles on `base-sepolia`. That is not a placeholder waiting
;; to be swapped for mainnet — it is the whole point of the file existing today.
;; A price that can be argued with has to be written down; a price that can be
;; charged has to pass gates that are not passed. Denominating in testnet USDC
;; makes the second impossible while the first is true, so this cannot start
;; earning real value by being forgotten.
;;
;; x402.nexus admits `base-sepolia` (nexus.apply/settleable-networks) and
;; announces it at /.well-known/x402 with `testnets: ["base-sepolia"]`, so a
;; paid path here can be demonstrated end to end without anyone transferring
;; value. That is why base-sepolia was added, and this is the first seller to
;; use it for what it was added for.
;;
;; ## The number is a floor, and it was measured, not chosen
;;
;; 2,338 credits over 246 finished video-seconds = 9.50 credits/second =
;; $0.095/second all-in (generation, voice, music, 3D assets, stills), from
;; GET https://api.murakumo.cloud/infer/runs on 2026-09-01 — a SNAPSHOT of a
;; live feed that moved from 1,858/186 to 2,338/246 within the same day. The model that
;; derives it and compares it against measured competitor prices is
;; `90-docs/system-dynamics/dougaka-unit-economics.cljs` in com-junkawasaki/root,
;; and it is an OASIS XMILE model so the arithmetic can be re-run rather than
;; believed.
;;
;; Break-even is therefore $0.095/second at that reading. Anything below it sells at a loss on
;; the compute alone, before anyone is paid for anything else.
;;
;; ## What the competitor numbers do and do not say
;;
;; fal.ai Wan 2.5 $0.05/s, Kling 2.5 Turbo Pro $0.07/s, Replicate wan-2 $0.09/s,
;; Replicate top published tier $0.25/s — all read from their own pricing pages
;; on 2026-09-01. **They are raw generation, not a finished short.** dougaka's
;; comparable figure is its generation-only rate, $0.0803/s, which sits between
;; Kling Turbo Pro and Replicate's wan-2. Quoting the all-in $0.0999 against
;; their $0.05 would be comparing a finished video to a model call.
;;
;; ## Margin is not computed here, because it is not computable
;;
;; ADR-2608291009 決定 5 defines margin as revenue − cost. Revenue is measured
;; and it is zero: no catalog entry names this seller. A margin of 0 for
;; `earned nothing` printing the same as `broke even` is the defect class
;; CLAUDE.md names, so the model reports MARGIN UNMEASURED and this file quotes
;; no percentage.

{:pricing/version 1
 :pricing/currency "USD"
 :pricing/settles-on "base-sepolia"
 :pricing/updated "2026-09-01"
 :pricing/authority "ADR-2608110200 (price as data) / ADR-2608291009 決定 5 (bot P&L)"
 :pricing/licence "licence.edn — 上流 7 モデルを実測した上で買い手に渡す条件"
 :pricing/availability "availability.edn — 稼働条件（約束ではなく実測）"
 :pricing/cost-basis
 {:measured-on "2026-09-01"
  :source "GET https://api.murakumo.cloud/infer/runs — 124 spend events, account `dougaka`"
  ;; ⚠ SNAPSHOT。この feed は生きていて、同じ日の数時間で 1,858/186 から
  ;; 2,338/246 へ動いた。**この数字を引用する前に model を回すこと** ——
  ;; model は feed を読み、ここには何も焼いていない。
  :credits 2338
  :finished-video-seconds 246
  :credits-per-video-second 9.5041
  :usd-per-video-second 0.095
  :generation-only-usd-per-video-second 0.0803
  :model "90-docs/system-dynamics/dougaka-unit-economics.cljs (com-junkawasaki/root)"}

 :pricing/plans
 [{:plan/id :per-second
   :plan/name "Finished vertical short, per second"
   :plan/status :proposed
   :plan/settles-on "base-sepolia"
   :plan/usd-per-video-second 0.15
   ;; 0.15 and not the ~0.095 floor: the floor is what the compute costs, and a price at
   ;; the floor funds no re-render, no failed take, and no storage. 0.15 leaves
   ;; 33% over the measured cost. It is a proposal — the number to argue with,
   ;; not a rate anyone has agreed.
   ;; Deliberately no margin percentage: margin needs revenue, revenue is
   ;; measured at zero, and a ratio computed against a cost alone is a markup,
   ;; not a margin. `:plan/markup-over-measured-cost` says what it is.
   :plan/markup-over-measured-cost 0.578
   :plan/hard-cap {:video-seconds 90}
   :plan/includes [:generation :voice :music :stills :edit :srt]}

  {:plan/id :per-short
   :plan/name "One finished short, up to 90 seconds"
   :plan/status :proposed
   :plan/settles-on "base-sepolia"
   :plan/usd 13.50
   ;; 90 × 0.15. Stated separately because a buyer asking for `a short` is not
   ;; asking for seconds, and a per-unit price a buyer can check against their
   ;; own budget is the one that does not get disputed.
   :plan/hard-cap {:videos 1}}]

 ;; ADR-2608110200 決定 4 の形。**通っていない gate は通っていないと書く。**
 :pricing/gates
 [{:gate/id :mainnet-denomination
   :gate/met? false
   :gate/detail "settles-on is base-sepolia. Charging real value needs a
                 deliberate change to `base` here and in every plan, which is
                 the point: forgetting cannot promote a testnet price."}
  {:gate/id :discovery-document
   :gate/met? false
   :gate/detail "dougaka serves no /.well-known/x402, so x402.nexus cannot read
                 this book. `nexus.apply/rules-from-document` registers what an
                 origin publishes about itself and nothing else."}
  {:gate/id :output-license
   :gate/met? false
   :gate/detail "STATED, NOT REVIEWED (2026-09-01). licence.edn now says what a
                 buyer receives, derived from all seven upstream models read the
                 same day: MiniMax's terms let the customer retain ownership of
                 generated content (which is what makes the 83% of credits spent
                 on minimax-h3 sellable at all), four open-weight models are
                 Apache-2.0/MIT, and animagine-xl-4.0's OpenRAIL++ flows
                 use-restrictions down to the buyer. The gate stays UNMET because
                 `:licence/status :proposed` — an agent measured the upstream and
                 wrote the terms; nobody qualified has reviewed them, and a
                 legal gate is not one an agent may flip."}
  {:gate/id :availability
   :gate/met? true
   :gate/met-on "2026-09-01"
   :gate/detail "availability.edn states the cadence (daily 10:30 tick, and that
                 the registry cadence is :active? false so the actor is not
                 currently running of its own accord), what a governor hold does
                 (no delivery, ledger-only), and that a held commission is not
                 charged — implemented as charge-AFTER-hold rather than refund,
                 because x402 is prepaid and settling first would leave a payer
                 with nothing. It is `:status :measured`, not a promise: the
                 known gaps (no delivery history, no measured latency) are named
                 in the same file."}]}
